    "title": "Rare bacterial infection in Edgartown prompts warnings - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sarah Shaw Dawson ,\n9 hours ago The Edgartown Board of Health is urging residents to exercise caution when swimming after a Vineyard resident over the age of 65 contracted a bacterial infection called Vibrio vulnificus, a type of flesh-eating bacteria, after swimming in multiple bodies of water in the town with an open cut on their foot. Read full article\n1",
